Point the Arxiozyma entry of PCAn v1.0 at the CDEIII motif file that ships with it.

Why this is needed. At commit a5fa46f (PCAn v1.0, Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.17293587)
the Arxiozyma entry of MotifsAndThresholds names CDEIII/CDEIII_Ktel_MEME.txt.
That file is not in the repository, not in PCAn.zip and not in the Zenodo
archive. FIMO cannot open it, writes no fimo.txt, and PCAn stops with a
FileNotFoundError, so no Arxiozyma assembly can be run as released.

Why this file. CDEIII/CDEIII_Arxiozyma_MEME.txt ships with PCAn, is used by no
entry, and contains a motif named CDEIII_Arxiozyma (26 bp, 88 sites). The
per-species table that ships with PCAn, ExpectedFalsePosFalseNegs.txt, lists
"Arxiozyma" as the CDEIII motif for all seven Arxiozyma species, with the same
thresholds as the code (1e-6 for CDEIII, 1e-3 for CDEI).

Nothing else changes. Every other entry, threshold and filter is as released.
scripts/01_install.sh applies this patch with git apply after checking out the
pinned commit, and records that it did so.

